UPDATE agent_issues SET updated_at = CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000, description = description || char(10) || char(10) ||
 'REM-A6 2026-10-26: the premise of the owner holding this issue is stale, and the issue has no consumer. qnfo-skill-sync was RETIRED on 2026-10-06 (its RETIRED file: it ran a kaizen cycle over chat_logs and never synced the skills mirror); the fleet graph shows r2:qnfo-skills read only through qnfo-ops''s generic r2 tools (binding SKILLS_R2), and skill_pull.py on the owner machine pulls from the GitHub repository QNFO/qnfo-skills, not from R2. So the mirror prompts/skills/ has no reader. A doer path exists server-side: the qnfo-ops agent can refresh it with github_repo_read and r2_put (qnfo-ops holds SKILLS_R2); scripts/cf_ops_actions.py has no R2 write action (r2-get only) and a session has no R2 write path. Decide: refresh once and schedule it, or record the mirror as unmaintained by successor goal; either closes this issue with evidence.'
