UPDATE agent_issues SET updated_at = CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000, description = description || char(10) || char(10) ||
 'REM-A6 2026-10-26: not worked in this session. It depends on issue 1000154: qnfo-fleet-control 0.56.1 (PR 4813) reads an HTTP 410 answer with a retired marker as a third state in the state snapshot and gives the stub a TOMBSTONE_410 worker_live_audit row, but the registry row of qnfo-workers is still state live (updated 2026-10-26 19:00Z), which is what this issue''s probe reads. Flipping it to retired without teaching the worker_count_disagreement check and workers_idle_7d the tombstone class makes the registry count 34 against 35 live scripts, as the issue says; the Workers Builds integration recreates the stub on every push, so the script cannot be deleted. Next: teach the disagreement check and workers_idle_7d the tombstone class, then set the registry state to retired.'
